interpretation: 'eff' is contraction GF/s divided by same-shape GEMM GF/s.
'eff ratio' is complex eff over real eff. Below 1.0 means the engine loses
more to overheads on complex data than on real data -- the headroom this
project targets. At or above 1.0 the complex-weakness thesis is refuted.

